  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="who-is-a-candidate">Who is a candidate — and when to see a specialist</h2>
<p>Choosing well means matching the treatment to the cause. The factors that matter most are the <strong>severity</strong> on your sleep study, your <strong>anatomy</strong> (nose, tonsils, palate, tongue and jaw position), your <strong>weight</strong>, the health of your <strong>teeth and jaw joints</strong>, other medical conditions, and what you are realistically willing to use or undergo. Many people end up with a combination — weight loss with an oral appliance, for example, or nasal surgery to make CPAP comfortable.</p>
<p>See a specialist if you have tried CPAP and stopped, if you use it but still feel sleepy, if your sleep apnea is severe and you want to explore surgery, or if you have a receding chin or bite problem along with snoring. At Gnathos Facial in Gachibowli, Hyderabad, we assess the jaws and airway, review your sleep study and work with sleep physicians and ENT colleagues. Any surgery takes place at NABH-accredited partner hospitals, and hospital treatment may be covered by cashless insurance, subject to policy terms and pre-authorisation. Learn more about <a href="/osa-treatment">sleep apnea surgery</a>, or read about the <a href="/blogs/sleep-apnea-symptoms-in-adults/">symptoms of sleep apnea in adults</a> if you have not yet been diagnosed.</p>
